    "title": "How to Find Missing Angles",
    "content": "<p>Key angle facts: <strong>angles on a straight line</strong> sum to \\(180°\\), <strong>angles at a point</strong> sum to \\(360°\\), <strong>vertically opposite angles</strong> are equal.</p><p>For <strong>parallel lines</strong>: alternate angles are equal (Z-shape), corresponding angles are equal (F-shape), co-interior (allied) angles sum to \\(180°\\) (C/U-shape).</p><p><strong>Triangle</strong> angles sum to \\(180°\\). <strong>Quadrilateral</strong> angles sum to \\(360°\\).</p><p>For any polygon with \\(n\\) sides: <strong>interior angle sum</strong> = \\((n - 2) \\times 180°\\). Each <strong>exterior angle</strong> of a regular polygon = \\(\\frac{360°}{n}\\).</p>",
    "example": "<p><strong>Find the interior angle of a regular octagon.</strong></p><p>Interior angle sum = \\((8 - 2) \\times 180 = 1080°\\)</p><p>Each angle = \\(1080 ÷ 8 = 135°\\)</p>"
  },
